Data binds via the shared P1/S8 `DriveScoreGaugeWidgetSource` seam (the production app wires the
`VehicleStore` active vehicle + the drive-score `Resource` + `SettingsStore`; previews/tests use the
in-memory source). No HTTP in the view. Web hooks reproduced: useVehicles, useDriveScore
(GET /drives/score?vehicle_id=), useTranslation.

Score bands ported verbatim from the web `SCORE_COLORS`/`scoreColor`: >=80 #10b981, >=60 #22d3ee,
>=40 #f59e0b, else #ef4444. Gauge readout = fmtNumber(clamped 0..100, integer→0 / else precision);
stat values + bar sublabels = bare JS `String(number)`; grade label falls back to em dash.

States reproduced from the web source (every state renders — no hidden surface):
  loading (skeleton), empty ("No score yet"), error (retry affordance), stale (chip + retained gauge,
  auto-refresh), offline (chip + cached gauge), content (gauge hero + 3 sub-score stats + 3 metric bars).

i18n keys (all from source, resolved through the P1/S10 facade; no English literals in code):
  widget.driveScoreGauge.{title,weekly,efficiency,smoothness,speed,noData} + description; plus
  native chrome (live/stale/offline/refresh/retry/loading/errorTitle/banners) + a11y templates.
Telemetry: `view.opened` (screen_view) with surface slug `DriveScoreGaugeWidget` (P1/S11 seam).

